# Line endings: text is LF in the repository AND in the working tree, whatever core.autocrlf says. Golden files, test data and
# generated output are compared byte for byte, so a CRLF checkout fails those tests (alamo_ai_tests, alamo_shaderxlat_tests did).
# Windows scripts are the exception: CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

# Binary files: never convert or diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.lib binary
*.zip binary
*.meg binary
*.bin binary
*.spv binary
*.ogg binary
*.wav binary
*.bik binary

